1. Definitions

"Personal Use" means use by an individual for personal, non-commercial projects,
learning, experimentation, or research, where the Software is not used for or on
behalf of any business, employer, client, government, nonprofit, or other
organization.

"Evaluation Use" means testing, trial, benchmarking, review, or proof-of-concept
use to decide whether to obtain a commercial license.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software for or on behalf of a business,
employer, client, government, nonprofit, or other organization, or any use that
is intended to generate revenue, reduce business operating costs, support a
commercial product or service, provide services to others, or support internal
business operations.

2. 15-Day Evaluation License

You may copy, install, run, test, and internally evaluate the Software, including
an evaluation performed for or on behalf of an organization, for no more than
15 calendar days. The period starts on the first day you or the organization
accesses, downloads, installs, runs, or otherwise uses the Software.

The evaluation limit is honor-based and is not technically enforced by the
Software. You are responsible for tracking the start date and stopping use when
the evaluation period expires.

After the 15-day Evaluation Use period ends, you must stop using the Software
unless your use qualifies as Personal Use or you have obtained a separate
commercial license.

